{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42581 - PROTEIN:6256",
  "verbalization": "Ferruginin B is linked to Histone H1.0 through a series of molecular targets that ultimately converge on this histone. The evidence suggests that Ferruginin B acts as a target for multiple compounds, all of which are classified as M-phase phosphoproteins. These phosphoproteins are in turn targets of various structurally diverse molecules, including (2S,3S)-2,3-Bis(5-Methoxy-3,4-Methylenedioxybenzyl)Butane-1,4-Diol Diacetate and (6S)-6-[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxyoctadecanoic acid, which share a common pathway of targeting Histone H1.0. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Ferruginin B may influence histone function through the modulation of M-phase-related proteins, possibly affecting chromatin structure and gene regulation. The consistent presence of these targets across different molecular structures suggests a broader role in histone modification or chromatin dynamics, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
